  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation bias: The model assumes a flat mean-reversion to ~70.50, but the market spiked to 76+ before crashing; apply a +4 to +6 EUR upward adjustment for the first 5-7 days of the forecast horizon.",
    "Implement aggressive mean reversion lag: The model fails to capture the rapid post-spike decline (76.67 to 67.23); reduce forecast slope immediately after day 5 to reflect a steeper downward trajectory rather than a slow drift.",
    "Invert sentiment signal for short-term spikes: A single positive sentiment (1.00) on day 6 preceded a price peak; treat isolated positive sentiment spikes as indicators of imminent local tops rather than sustained uptrends.",
    "Adjust for volatility clustering: The model's constant incremental growth ignores the high volatility observed in the true outcome; replace the linear forecast with a decaying curve that drops 2-3 EUR per week after the initial peak."
  ]
}
